{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Rice Cookout", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Will", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange advice and suggestions in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The First Conditional vs. The Second Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>You use the first conditional to talk about real situations in the present or future.</p><p>You use the second conditional to talk about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "First conditional form:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Simple Present verb, + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">If you come over, I'll help you with that.</span><br/>(you can come over)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Second conditional form:<br/><span class=\"italic\">If</span> + Simple Past verb,    + <span class=\"italic\">would</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">If you had time, I would help you with that.</span> <br/>(I don't think or I know you don't have time)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">First Conditional <br/>(Cause and Effect)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Second Conditional <br/>(Hypothetical Situations)</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If you overcook food it will be less exciting to eat.</p><p>If we warm up our food again, won't it be overcooked?</p><p>If you try out a dish, slice up the vegetables nice and thick so they'll cook slower.</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>If you learned to cook more dishes, you wouldn't always be hungry.</p><p>If we both learned a bit more, Peter, we could whip up some food together.</p><p>If we made something from Vanessa's blog we could take a picture and post it.</p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the <span class=\"italic\">IF</span> clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (<span class=\"italic\">I would</span> = <span class=\"italic\">I'd</span>).", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future With <span class=\"italic\">Will</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Going to</span>, and the<span class=\"italic\"> Present Simple", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use three different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are scheduled, like programs, classes, busses or trains, you use the Present Simple tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Deciding Now</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>I'll try that.</p><p>They'll still be crunchy!</p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Intentions</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>You guys are actually going to do up your own food! </p><p>I'm going to cook them less? </p></span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Schedules</span></div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><p>It comes on in the early evening right?</p><p>It starts again next weekend and plays from 1:00 to 3:00. </p></span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to whip up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make quickly and easily", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How did you whip up that dessert so quickly?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to do up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to create; package; put together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You could have someone else do up your meal!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to slice up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cut with a sharp knife", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Use this disc to slice up the vegetables with the food processor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to post", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put on a website", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm going to post these pictures on my website.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to try out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to experiment with; to test", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm trying out different dishes this weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to warm up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make hotter", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This one can warm up cold food too!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overcooked", "type": "name"}, {"content": "cooked too much", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: No more overcooked vegetables!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le18ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Decide on some activities you want to do on the weekend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down a plan of the activities you would like to do and when. (Use simple present, e.g. <span class=\"italic\">On Saturday, I meet Sarah at 10.</span>)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell someone about your plans.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I choose some activities to do on the weekend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a plan for the weekend.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about my plans.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le18ob11re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le18ob11re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn7le18ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"image": "engenn7le18ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I have been looking forward to this dinner all week!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: If you learned to cook more dishes, you wouldn't always be hungry.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: If we both learned a bit more, Peter, we could whip up some food together.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I've heard on the news that overcooked food dulls your appetite.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I'm not sure about that. Although, if you overcook food it will be less exciting to eat.", "time": "100", "id": 1}, {"image": "engenn7le18ob11re2img05.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: If we warm up our food again, won't it be overcooked?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: No. If you try out a dish, slice up the vegetables nice and thick so they'll cook slower. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Uh-huh.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Then they're going to cook less? They'll still be crunchy!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Right.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: My cooking experiment starts tomorrow.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: I'll be coming over to help.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Work starts at noon. Don't be late!", "time": "17550", "id": 2}, {"image": "engenn7le18ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You guys are actually going to do up your own food! I'm impressed!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: If we made something from Vanessa's blog we could take a picture and post it. If you comment on it, V, it will give other people the idea. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You should do that! <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: You can tell me how to make the dish so that I can cook it even better!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Will you do that for me then?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Sure. You pick out the easiest recipes and we'll try it.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That sounds like fun!", "time": "35450", "id": 3}]}}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about future actions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about cause and effects and hypothetical situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"conte